{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/13745-a-discussion-of-supernatural-energy-resources","id":13745,"title":"A Discussion of Supernatural Energy Resources","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-18T19:39:40-08:00","id":13745,"title":"A Discussion of Supernatural Energy Resources","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I need help understanding the various supernatural energy resources in the World of Darkness.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I think Essence is the natural energy of the world, and pervades just about everything. Ghosts use it, Spirits use it, God-Machine Angels use it, and it can be claimed by Werewolves from both a spirit locus and by the consumption of human flesh. We know of a direct link between Essence and another energy resource; Aether, the waste produced by the God-Machine's refining of Essence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">A few other energy resources interest me - Vitae, Pyros, and Plasm - with how they are related to Essence, and I suppose this is where I need help.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Essence is pervasive, but generally invisible to mortal humans. It is within them, however (see; Werewolves gain Essence by consuming human flesh) and is open to them once they die (and they become Ghosts). Vitae, then, is the Essence within a living human, perhaps refined by a Kindred's supernatural chemistry. Or maybe I am missing something?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Plasm can be gained by a Sin-Eater either by lurking in a place tainted by death (we can assume a Haunt is similar to a locus, albeit with a tie to the Underworld rather than the Shadow) or by fooling about with ghosts in a number of ways. Plasm seems to be either tainted or refined Essence; I can't tell if the tie is to the Underworld, or if the Geist within a Sin-Eater's body changes Essence even as it is absorbed. Many questions,a nd i have no answers.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Pyros is very strange, and seems to be wholly separate from Essence. It is described as rare, and seems to only exist within Prometheans and Qashmallim. Prometheans can convert mundane energies into Pyros, and are themselves powered by it, though in the refined form of Azoth. It is a dynamic power source, and can be tainted (Elpis or Flux). Where does it come from? It seems to be completely unnatural.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">My only hint of a theory towards Pyros ties into the Gnostic theories proposed towards the Principle and the God-Machine; that the Principle fits as the &quot;true god&quot; and has a unique power source, while the God-Machine is the false demiurge and uses the Essence that is common in the physical world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This has been a long and meandering post, but I wanted to put this out here and hear from others as well. Discussion of just what Gnosis, Glamour, and Sekhem are would also be welcome.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T20:12:31-08:00","id":13751,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/13745-a-discussion-of-supernatural-energy-resources#post13745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plasm can be gained by a Sin-Eater either by lurking in a place tainted by death (we can assume a Haunt is similar to a locus, albeit with a tie to the Underworld rather than the Shadow) or by fooling about with ghosts in a number of ways. Plasm seems to be either tainted or refined Essence; I can't tell if the tie is to the Underworld, or if the Geist within a Sin-Eater's body changes Essence even as it is absorbed. Many questions,a nd i have no answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding has generally been that plasm is essentially ghost-Corpus and/or the stuff the Underworld is made of; Oppia has great nets for catching the upwellings of Essence that rise from the depths of the Underworld, but there doesn't seem to be a brisk trade in plasm among the dead.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pyros is very strange, and seems to be wholly separate from Essence. It is described as rare, and seems to only exist within Prometheans and Qashmallim. Prometheans can convert mundane energies into Pyros, and are themselves powered by it, though in the refined form of Azoth. It is a dynamic power source, and can be tainted (Elpis or Flux). Where does it come from? It seems to be completely unnatural. </div> </div> </div>Completely unnatural and completely natural, is the thing. Look up the Tao and see what one of the possible translations of the word is.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T20:27:29-08:00","id":13754,"title":"","content":"Apparently:<br /> \u201cWerewolves recognize in Glamour a close cousin to the Essence they collect and use for their own purposes. Both are forms of energy created by abstract concepts such as emotions, but the difference is that Essence can come from many sources apart from emotions\u201d<br /> \u201cMages see Glamour as a curious sort of blend of the Essence that fuels the Shadow and the Mana that trickles down into the Fallen World from the Supernal.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T20:51:23-08:00","id":13761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/13745-a-discussion-of-supernatural-energy-resources?p=13754#post13754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently:<br /> \u201cWerewolves recognize in Glamour a close cousin to the Essence they collect and use for their own purposes. Both are forms of energy created by abstract concepts such as emotions, but the difference is that Essence can come from many sources apart from emotions\u201d<br /> \u201cMages see Glamour as a curious sort of blend of the Essence that fuels the Shadow and the Mana that trickles down into the Fallen World from the Supernal.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Moreover, mages can manipulate Glamour with Fate magic in the same manner as Essence is manipulated with Spirit, and substitute it for Mana on Fate or Time spells (at the rate of two Glamour points per one Mana).<br /> <br /> As for what Glamour actually is in the <i>CtL</i> line, well, &quot;the distilled essence of human emotion&quot; is the basic definition. Just about everyone who isn't fae generates this energy naturally into their surroundings during emotional moments, where it then rapidly dissipates unless harvested by the fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">(Previously known by the name of &quot;GrimGent&quot;.)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/335-the-yann-waters","name":"The Yann Waters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T03:35:14-08:00","id":13913,"title":"","content":"It always seemed tome that Glamour and Plasm were very refined and focused varieties of Essence, Emotion-resonant Essence in the case of Glamour and Death-resonant Essence in the case of Plasm. Mana is something like Supernal Essence in that it suposedly permeates everything and can have a wide range of Resonances equal to those of Essence, the difference being that Essence is generated in the Phenomenal world and Mana comes from the Supernal.<br /> Vitae is the odd one out, but it could very well be that blood (and Blood) is the physical medium or seat of the Essence that flows through living beings, Life-resonant Essence.<br /> <br /> Pyros is a Mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T08:44:05-08:00","id":14079,"title":"","content":"That discussion kinda reminds me of the &quot;Theory of Everything&quot; from physics.. I like seeing each &quot;supernatural energy&quot; as a seperated form of energy, with each splat thinking that theirs is the &quot;the best and most refined&quot; form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T09:08:24-08:00","id":14092,"title":"","content":"I think the idea that Essence is the &quot;core&quot; energy is somewhat flawed. Granted, that's just my personal take and has more to do with how I feel about far broader concepts like religion, faith, science, and mysticism.<br /> <br /> I feel like there's some kind of underlying, &quot;core&quot; energy that moves the World of Darkness. Call it the God Particle (but not around a physicist), Super Strings, The Force, The Schwartz, or the Flying Spaghetti Monster's Secret Sauce, but this is the fundamental mystical energy that makes the World of Darkness function. Everything we see in splats are 'fragments' or aspects of that energy, either altered by passing through different filters or simply called something else because it is being observed from a different perspective.<br /> <br /> Essence is this energy as distilled through the Spirit world and animistic concept of the Shadow. Essence is what it is and does what it does because the Shadow is what it is, and uses the energy in the way it does. Think of the Shadow as a still, and the Energy is grain and water poured into the still. They come out as something very different then when they went in. The Energy the Shadow uses becomes Essence because the Shadow uses it.<br /> <br /> Vitae is quite simply the life force of human beings, concentrated by the vampire's own undead body into a more potent form. Think of it like &quot;life extract.&quot; A vampire doesn't need the red corpuscles and platelets and plasma. They just need the force of life. The mystical energy that gives Vitae (and human blood, for that matter) its unique characteristics is the same energy that becomes Essence when it fuels the Shadow, but in this case is filtered through the biological processes of a living organism and that strange magic of &quot;being alive,&quot; creating this mystical, distilled extract of life. When vampires consume blood and turn it into Vitae, they filter and modify it yet again, creating a new energetic substance.<br /> <br /> Mana is the Energy that runs the Supernal World, and like the Shadow, the Supernal alters that energy because of how it makes use of it. The Mana that exists in the Fallen World is somewhat tainted by its passage through the Abyss (if I recall my Mage correctly), making it something yet again different from Supernal Mana.<br /> <br /> Pyros is tricky. Since Pyros is both the Divine Fire itself, as well as the energy it gives off. Azoth and Flux are the opposing forces of the Divine Fire, creation and destruction. Pyros itself could be likened to the &quot;heat&quot; the Divine Fire gives off, harnessed to generate power. Pyros is the flame generated by the Divine Fire burning the Energy to sustain itself.<br /> <br /> Glamour is again a byproduct of that magical process of &quot;being alive.&quot; The Energy that gives all living things that spark of magic is again filtered through their brains and minds, and releases the intangible light of Glamour in bursts of emotion.<br /> <br /> Plasm is interesting, in that it is partially a substance, ectoplasm, that which gives ghosts a Corpus. But Plasm as Bound use it is something else yet again. As Blood and Vitae are two different &quot;phases&quot; of the same &quot;energy state,&quot; so too are ectoplasm and Plasm. The Energy that runs the Underworld becomes this substance, and like the dead themselves, and leak into our world, where it can be harvested by the Bound.<br /> <br /> Anyway, call that my two cents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T10:31:15-08:00","id":14154,"title":"","content":"For my games, I usually place Pyros as the &quot;prime particle&quot;. It's the natural ebb &amp; flow of creation and destruction, a force of change and cannot be detected, duplicated or harnessed easily (if at all) by any of the other splats. All other forms are different spectrum as seen thru the prism of their respective splat. Viate is filtered thru the Curse and the Blood of vampirism, Essence is filtered thru the Shadow Realm, Mana thru the Supernal, Glamour thru dreams and the Wyrd, Plasm thru death and the Underworld, Sekhem thru &quot;un-death&quot; and the spells of Irem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T11:43:59-08:00","id":14205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Essence is pervasive, but generally invisible to mortal humans. It is within them, however (see; Werewolves gain Essence by consuming human flesh)</span></span> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say werewolf feeding proves that there is Essence in humans, I would've said werewolves regain Essence by acting out their &quot;hunter&quot; nature just like a fire spirit feeds from a real fire, except werewolves are limited to feeding from wolves and humans because they're unnatural hybrids of spirit and flesh that should not be. From the point of view of the spiritual world, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T12:40:49-08:00","id":14225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/13745-a-discussion-of-supernatural-energy-resources?p=14205#post14205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say werewolf feeding proves that there is Essence in humans, I would've said werewolves regain Essence by acting out their &quot;hunter&quot; nature just like a fire spirit feeds from a real fire, except werewolves are limited to feeding from wolves and humans because they're unnatural hybrids of spirit and flesh that should not be. From the point of view of the spiritual world, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;when Max Roman found the underground lake that led to the idigam\u2019s downfall, he saw the world from Gurdilag\u2019s perspective. He saw thousands of pinpricks of light, like stars in a clear night sky, some shining brighter than others. He realized with horror that the lights represented the world\u2019s Essence, and the brighter lights were loci, powerful spirits\u2026and werewolves. The smaller lights were human beings, their souls calling out to the idigam in the same way that the vast expanse of space might intrigue a human philosopher, explorer or profiteer&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T13:52:36-08:00","id":14267,"title":"","content":"well, it says the human SOULS are made of Essence- which is kinda logical. It says nothing about their physical body- and as far as I remember, the werewolves eat the body, not the soul. This is Tremere's territory.<br /> <br /> Edit- In short, I think that werewolves gain essence from eating humans and wolves because of the principle of the Shadow, meaning &quot;eat something similar to you in order to become stronger&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T14:39:38-08:00","id":14299,"title":"","content":"Mind, Soul and Spirit<br /> The process of becoming one of the purified involves a character projecting her spiritual essence outside of her body and having it transformed in the Shadow Realm. While this essence is referred to as the character\u2019s mind, it actually consists of her mind and her soul, both of which are transformed when she becomes one of the purified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T15:05:16-08:00","id":14316,"title":"","content":"Ok.. so mind, soul and spirit are the essence.. doesn't werewolves still eat only the body?<br /> <br /> (that discussion is starting to get a little creepy..)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T15:38:25-08:00","id":14336,"title":"","content":"It's a big Harmony sin to do the eating thing, but I suppose what it boils down to is by eating them they are eating the essence of them, including a mix of soul and mind and body. Being spiritual creatures, their devouring is not merely a physical thing.<br /> <br /> As further support to it not being about the hunt (though I can understand where the idea comes from), werewolves don't get essence from eating vampires or mages, both of whom have souls but have souls that are irrevocably altered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T16:51:56-08:00","id":14372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/13745-a-discussion-of-supernatural-energy-resources?p=14336#post14336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As further support to it not being about the hunt (though I can understand where the idea comes from), werewolves don't get essence from eating vampires or mages, both of whom have souls but have souls that are irrevocably altered.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, werewolves can recover Essence by eating the flesh of changelings, who don't have enough of a human soul left to, say, maintain a spiritual connection to the Watchtowers (which is the in-setting reason why the Lost can't Awaken).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">(Previously known by the name of &quot;GrimGent&quot;.)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/335-the-yann-waters","name":"The Yann Waters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T17:04:17-08:00","id":14381,"title":"","content":"well, I assume that the only way to know for sure is to find if there is something about if people who are eaten by werewolves leave ghosts behind.. I mean, if they eat the soul/ mind/ spirit with the body, there shouldn't be a ghost left behind, right?<br /> <br /> Is there something about that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T17:04:37-08:00","id":14382,"title":"","content":"And interestingly enough, the Essence werewolves get from it has a strong resonance to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T23:07:58-08:00","id":14550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/13745-a-discussion-of-supernatural-energy-resources?p=14336#post14336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As further support to it not being about the hunt (though I can understand where the idea comes from), werewolves don't get essence from eating vampires or mages, both of whom have souls but have souls that are irrevocably altered.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where the &quot;unnatural hybrid that should not be&quot; part comes in. Only having the option to feed on those that are kin to you (humans and wolves) is the kind of sucky thing that happens when you're a monster and your innate spiritual nature does not express itself in the natural manner. As you say, mages and vampire are not normal humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T21:40:07-08:00","id":15116,"title":"","content":"Where is it said that werewolves don't get essence from eating mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T22:45:09-08:00","id":15151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/13745-a-discussion-of-supernatural-energy-resources?p=15116#post15116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is it said that werewolves don't get essence from eating mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I don't remember this. If Changelings give essence then so should juicy witch Flesh!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T01:41:19-08:00","id":15244,"title":"","content":"Mages are humans, period. If a werewolf eats some grilled Obrimos for dinner he should get Essence from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T07:09:44-08:00","id":15349,"title":"","content":"In the Werewolf core book.<br /> <br /> A werewolf who eats wolf or human \ufb02esh (including<br /> that of wolf-blooded humans, a vampire\u2019s ghouls or a mage\u2019s<br /> acolytes) regains one point of Essence for every point of<br /> damage in\ufb02icted with the intention of devouring the victim\u2019s<br /> meat. This is a grave sin that can lead to a loss of Harmony<br /> <br /> Presumably it's because the souls of Mages are altered by their Awakening, just like the souls of vampires are changed by the Embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-21-2013, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T07:14:05-08:00","id":15351,"title":"","content":"Note that when it says &quot;acolyte&quot; there, it means &quot;Sleepwalker&quot;. Possibly &quot;Proximus&quot;.<br /> <br /> Basically, the design of Mage's associated near-normals changed between the Forsaken core and the Awakening core coming out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T09:58:41-08:00","id":15446,"title":"","content":"I see Glamour as the reality-supporting Essence of certain types of possible ways the world could be if it were constructed differently, i.e. in a more Arcadian manner. It does not exist in the Fallen World in our timeline, but Changelings' property of being pulled out of the boundaries of our Time/Fate give them access to the possible-but-not supernatural structure/energy of the events that happen in our world. In other words, they're drawing Essence from disparate timelines, except that in those places where Fate is Wyrd, time doesn't come in lines, and its natural energy is free to flow according to Glamour-moving events in our world. From our world's point of view, though, things that happen are completely separate from things that could have been but aren't, so the causal flow is one-way: Our world affects otherworldly Glamour, but it doesn't provide feedback to our Fate the way the Shadow does until the Fae intrude in a more deliberate and local manner. Therefore, notwithstanding Legacies or Archmastery, even if a (post-Fall?) Mage could manipulate and even create Glamour, I don't think they could ever perceive the flow that Changelings normally harvest from, and they learn nothing of its nature from Awakening to the Watchtower-centered aspect of Arcadia that shines on our timeline.<br /> <br /> Except when it doesn't work like that, and it shouldn't, but maybe it could, but probably not, but what does &quot;probably not&quot; even mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T10:10:59-08:00","id":15455,"title":"","content":"Wow, I like it. Certainly makes the Keepers a more intimidating force, and would cause to explain the madness resonance with glamour/essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:21:16-08:00","id":15571,"title":"","content":"High Glamour is also noted to affect one's perceptions in a way similar to low Clarity and high Wyrd, and it has been suggested (by fans) in forum discussions that Changeling hallucinations are not merely the hallucination of things as being more fae, but being actual, accurate perceptions of ways the world could be but isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T19:41:17-08:00","id":15810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/13745-a-discussion-of-supernatural-energy-resources?p=14092#post14092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vitae is quite simply the life force of human beings, concentrated by the vampire's own undead body into a more potent form. Think of it like &quot;life extract.&quot; A vampire doesn't need the red corpuscles and platelets and plasma. They just need the force of life. The mystical energy that gives Vitae (and human blood, for that matter) its unique characteristics is the same energy that becomes Essence when it fuels the Shadow, but in this case is filtered through the biological processes of a living organism and that strange magic of &quot;being alive,&quot; creating this mystical, distilled extract of life. When vampires consume blood and turn it into Vitae, they filter and modify it yet again, creating a new energetic substance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though, Kindred are able to transmute Vitae into Essence (via the second-tier ability of Blood Tenebrous) as well as transmute Essence into Vitae (directly from a ghost's anchors (via the Ghost Eater merit in <i>Book of the Dead</i>) or indirectly through ectoplasm (via the second-tier ability of Essentiaphagia)), as well as derive extra Vitae (5:2 ratio) from Uratha blood (which ostensibly has a greater Essence-to-volume ratio than mortal blood) &amp; experience hallucinogenic &quot;trips&quot; from Mage or Changling blood, and gain additional abilities from consuming certain Essence-based materials (e.g. consuming another Kindred's soul via Diablerie or consuming a ghost via the fifth-tier ability of Essentiaphagia) - all of which would seem to imply some substantial link between Vitae and Essence.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, how many (if any) of the feeding-from-other-template effects will be carried over to B&amp;S?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Mortal</b><br /> Feeding from a mortal is pretty much a given considering this is how vampires survive.<br /> <br /> Effects: In most cases mortals do not resist the ecstasy of the bite. Therefore they go into a state of shock feeling bliss. Depending on the level of success for the feeding vampire, a mortal may have no memory of what happened.<br /> <br /> <b>The Werewolf</b><br /> Effects: The Werewolf's experience is identical to that of a mundane mortal.<br /> <br /> Result: The Vampire learns that the ferocious blood of Werewolves is over two times as nourishing but distills some of their aggression into the imbibing Vampire leading to a greater risk of frenzying for a number of nights equal to health boxes 'drained' from the Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <b>The Vampire</b><br /> Effects: Kindred do not succumb to the kiss since they know what is going on. They can fight back if they so inclined. Feeding until the subject dies is called diablerie.<br /> <br /> <b>The Mage</b><br /> Effects: Mages are just as tasty and filling as any other mortal. They also react the same way to being nommed. Although they are not all that high on the menu since their blood is rumored to be quite hallucinogenic to kindred. Whether they see the reality only known to mages or if it truly is a hallucination is not known, but most vampires are not that eager to find out. Those that do risk suffer a derangement per night for each vitae drained.<br /> <br /> <b>The Changeling</b><br /> Effects: Changlings are the same as mortals when it comes to experiencing the kiss. However, as a vampire drinks from a Changling they begin to become affected by the Changling's particular influence - Seeming, Kith, Wyrd, Glamour, and Clarify all play a roll in the 'hallucinogenic trip' the vampire experiences but the system is the same.<br /> <br /> For the rest of the night the vampire is at a -1 penalty to Perception for each point of Changling blood in their system and that day the vampire will actually dream, vividly. The next night the penalty is no more as the effect is 'slept off' during the day-dreams.<br /> <br /> The Changling's blood tastes very good and contains strong emotions which the vampire might very well enjoy, however the delusions become stronger in intensity as the feeding continues which will likely cause the vampire to break off before killing the victim. This can be expressed as a self control roll if they wish to continue to drink from the Changling for more traits worth than the vampire has points in Resolve. This roll is also penalized by the modifier for having the glamoured blood in their system.<br /> <br /> <b>The Promethean</b><br /> Effects: Now the Prometheans are immune to the overwhelming nature of the kiss. With the fact that the life blood, Azoth, is only half as nourishing as mortal blood AND does not taste very good. Most vampires wouldn't even bother viewing them as a &quot;Grade D&quot; but edible food source.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sin-Eater</b><br /> Effects: There doesn't seem to be any difference between a Mortal and a Sin-Eater, as far as their blood is concerned. However, many of the Caul Manifestations have a dramatic effect on the body of the Sin-Eater, and thus could render his blood unpalatable. While not as low as Prometheans on the menu, they're probably almost as risky a food source as Mages. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/212-stormbringer","name":"Stormbringer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T15:08:47-08:00","id":16818,"title":"","content":"Well, Vitae is only achieved <i>after</i> the vampire ingests regular blood. Therefore, I believe that whatever the vampiric curse is, it turns Life-essence into Death-essence<br /> <br /> Pyros is Empyrean-essence. Something far purer than mana.<br /> <br /> Btw, it could be useful to list all the ways to turn one supernatural-fuel into another. For example, some disciplines allow for vitae &lt;-&gt; essence conversion. Same goes for mana and essence.<br /> <br /> I'd say that all juices can become essence (save, perhaps, pyros because the empyrean can't be processed/understood)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T15:19:29-08:00","id":16821,"title":"","content":"A Promethean can also spend Pyros to give the companion (it's the spirit companion merit) Essence, channeling the Divine Fire through his ectoplasmic humour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T16:12:42-08:00","id":16854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-